    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1332-a1">

                <pb facs="0898" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg782"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Peláez to the oil companies.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nationalist Army, Peláez Brigade</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Temapache</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 7, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The undersigned, General in Chief of the Villista forces operating in the
                    Huasteca region, imposes on the Compañía de Petroleo “El Aguila” a forced
                    contribution for troop expenses of $100,000 (one hundred thousand pesos), which
                    the General Superintendent of said company will please pay in to these
                    Headquarters within the term of eight days.</p>
                <p>The above company is also advised that, from now on, all taxes which the
                    so-called Carrancista Government may have imposed upon it must be paid into
                    these Headquarters, with the understanding that it cannot excuse itself from
                    such payments even though it may claim to have made them to some authority
                    appointed by said Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">General Manuel Peláez</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
